  {
   "name": "mart_opportunity_bridge",
   "rows": 6,
   "description": "The closing visual, and deliberately not a year on year variance bridge. Kestrel's findings are standing costs rather than deterioration: empty returns, doors that will not receive, thirsty trucks and a service clause were all just as true last year. Framing them as variance would be dishonest and produces a meaningless residual. So this runs the other way. It starts at what Kestrel actually earned and adds what each finding identified, ending at what the same fleet and the same customers could contribute with nothing new bought. The figures are what the findings are worth in full; recovery…",
